# Vocabulary closure

The resolve engine implements the gates and deltas in `VOCAB.md` — **all of
them, only them.** Unknown words fail at **load time**, never silently at play
time, and the error names the path to the offending node.

## the words

Gates — all listed must hold; a response with no gate is the fallback, and
every action must end with one:

```
flags: [id, ...]      all set on the run
items: [id, ...]      all currently carried
```

Deltas, applied in VOCAB order; all optional except `say`:

```
say · set · give · take · journal · refuse · goto · addObject · removeObject · end
```

`refuse: true` logs to the refused ledger and **implies no other delta fired**.
`addObject`/`removeObject` carry `{scene, object, cause}` and are the only legal
way a scene's object set changes.

## reserved

`contest` (dice) · `dropObols` (death) · `prompt` (QTE) · `roll` (chance gate) ·
`counter` (economies) · `lies` (sanity).

**Do not implement these and do not use them.** Each arrives as its own
amendment card in P2 — one word, its tests, its lint, one system per wave.

A new word is never an inline special case. If your card needs a word that is
not here, you do not add it — you bounce (AGENTS.md).
